        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Minh Diep",
          "email": "mdiep@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-25 17:28:49.000000000",
          "tz": -480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21334 utils: leave md stripe_cache_size alone by default",
        "message": "LU-21334 utils: leave md stripe_cache_size alone by default\n\nmount.lustre defaulted md_stripe_cache_size to 16384, so every md\ndevice under an OST was raised to 16384 stripe heads at each mount.\nEach head holds one page per member device, so this cost about\n285 MiB for a 4-member array and 670 MiB for a 10-member array, and\nthe md driver could not shrink below it.  A 2 GiB server with four\narrays lost 1.14 GiB to stripe caches, then mount.lustre failed with\n\"page allocation failure: order:4\" and netlink returned ENOBUFS.\n\nChange the default to 0, so the device keeps its own value unless\n-o md_stripe_cache_size=<num> sets one.  Document the sizing rule in\nmount.lustre(8) for sites with md RAID5/6 over HDDs that need a larger\ncache: a 10-member RAID6 with 8 writers of 4 MiB lost 52% of its write\nthroughput at 256 compared with 16384.  Also fix the man page: the\nvalue is a count of stripe heads, not KiB, and only OST devices are\ntuned.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nTLC-bug-id: TLU-298\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\nChange-Id: Id4ceb955e0f95aba46e1cee1c8b365212865642b\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
